//
// LEGAL POSITIONING NOTE — READ BEFORE EDITING:
// Bulgaria is a PERMISSION-BY-COMMISSION tier market. The route
// exists at parental request — unlike Croatia — but it is granted
// by a regional commission and supervised every term.
// - The framework is САМОСТОЯТЕЛНА ФОРМА НА ОБУЧЕНИЕ (independent
//   form of education) under the Preschool and School Education Act
//   (ЗПУО). It consists of INDEPENDENT PREPARATION plus EXAMS to
//   determine annual grades in the subjects of the school curriculum
//   (училищен учебен план) — the day-form curriculum applies.
// - WHO IT IS ORGANISED FOR (state all three accurately):
//   1. Students of compulsory school age who, for health reasons
//      certified by the relevant medical expert commission, cannot
//      study in the day form. (Factual only — not a pathway.)
//   2. Students of compulsory school age — AT THE REQUEST of the
//      student or parent under Art. 12(2) ЗПУО — FOLLOWING A
//      DECISION OF AN EXPERT COMMISSION established at the REGIONAL
//      EDUCATION DIRECTORATE (РУО). This is the parental route.
//   3. Students who have passed compulsory school age (see window).
// - THE OVERSIGHT IS THE DISTINCTIVE PART, ALWAYS STATE IT: for the
//   parent-request category, under Art. 112(7) ЗПУО the РУО expert
//   commission — WHICH INCLUDES A REPRESENTATIVE OF THE SOCIAL
//   ASSISTANCE AGENCY — exercises control EACH SCHOOL TERM over the
//   organisation and conduct of the examination sessions and over
//   their results. Termly supervision by a body including social
//   services is unusual in our coverage and families deserve to
//   know it before applying, not after.
// - MECHANICS: the school organises the examination sessions;
//   students apply to sit at least ~10 days before a session; the
//   school provides consultation hours; and — important — a student
//   may only sit exams for the NEXT grade if they have SUCCESSFULLY
//   PASSED ALL exams for the previous grade. Mid-year switching
//   into the independent form is allowed for students turning 16
//   that year or on newly arisen circumstances, but NOT for the
//   parent-request category — so that route is a start-of-year
//   decision. Naredba No. 10/2016 and No. 11 govern the detail;
//   always tell families to confirm current rules with their school
//   and their РУО.
// - CONSEQUENCE FOR POSITIONING: the exams and the commission are
//   the family's relationship with their school and РУО. We are the
//   ACADEMIC SPINE beside that, or — simpler for most expat
//   families — SUPPLEMENTARY beside an ordinary day-form enrolment,
//   which needs no commission at all. Never imply we can satisfy,
//   replace, or shortcut the commission route.
// - Bulgarian-language and national-curriculum coverage must run all
//   year for any family in самостоятелна форма (the Serbia/Slovenia
//   discipline).
// - THE WINDOW: compulsory school age in Bulgaria ends at 16. After
//   that the independent form is available to students in their own
//   right, and the compulsory obligation is over — so the A-Level
//   years sit outside it. Use prominently but accurately: the
//   independent form still involves school exams if a student stays
//   inside the Bulgarian system; a student outside it has no
//   Bulgarian obligation at all.
// MARKET NOTE: the international tier is a Sofia story — the
// Anglo-American School of Sofia, the American College of Sofia,
// Zlatarski International School, St George International School and
// peers, plus the French, German and Italian lycées. Plovdiv, Varna
// and Burgas have very little; Ruse and the mountains have none.
// Economy: a large IT and outsourcing sector (Sofia, Plovdiv,
// Varna), the Trakia Economic Zone around Plovdiv with its
// international manufacturers, Black Sea ports and tourism at Varna
// and Burgas, the Danube corridor at Ruse (Bucharest an hour away),
// and Bansko — one of Europe's best-known digital-nomad and ski
// destinations. Large diaspora in Germany, Spain, the UK and the US.
// TIMEZONE — NOT THE CET FRAMING: Bulgaria runs EET (UTC+2) / EEST
// (UTC+3 summer) — 0-1 hours behind Nairobi EAT, and in summer Sofia
